  "notes": "The Tudor Great Gatehouse and moat bridge open into Base Court, with Anne Boleyn’s Gateway and the astronomical clock between it and Clock Court. The Great Hall and Chapel Royal rooflines meet the Baroque east front, Fountain Court arcades and the northern Royal Tennis Court range. The palace perimeter, seven court voids, named hall and chapel footprints, and three mapped passage centerlines use PMTiles. Standard viewer terrain determines the gate, bridge and court levels. Roof pitches, chimney positions, window subdivisions, the heraldic stonework and the astronomical dial are exterior reconstructions from ordinary photographs. The fountain is static and rooms beyond the open passages and cloister are outside the scope.",
