    "notes": "OSM relation 21104 and the mapped hall and chapel fit the site. Model +X runs from the Tudor west gate toward the Baroque garden façade. All three mapped gate paths and independent features remain in the viewer. The palace perimeter, seven court voids, named hall and chapel footprints, and three mapped passage centerlines use PMTiles. Standard viewer terrain determines the gate, bridge and court levels. Roof pitches, chimney positions, window subdivisions, the heraldic stonework and the astronomical dial are exterior reconstructions from ordinary photographs. The fountain is static and rooms beyond the open passages and cloister are outside the scope."
  },
